<title>USA: Motorola cuts prices on &quot;StarMax&quot; systems.</title>
<headline>Motorola cuts prices on &quot;StarMax&quot; systems.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc's Motorola Computer Group said Tuesday it had cut prices on its &quot;StarMax&quot; line of Macintosh-compatible computer systems.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that since shipping began in mid-November, over 56,000 StarMax units have been sold.</p>
<p>&quot;We continue to pursue our goal to further expand the Mac market,&quot; said spokesman Dennis Schneider.</p>
<p>&quot;By continuing to offer better payload at more attractive prices ... we will provide customers with the best Mac-compatible system value available in the market today,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>Effective immediately, the following are the manufacturers' suggested resale street prices for the StarMax product line in the U.S.</p>
<p>Model				 Previous   New	Difference</p>
<p>StarMax 3000/160 Desktop	$1,495     $1,249     $246</p>
<p>StarMax 3000/160 Minitower    $1,795     $1,399     $396</p>
<p>StarMax 3000/180 Desktop	$1,595     $1,395     $200</p>
<p>StarMax 3000/180 Minitower    $1,895     $1,595     $300</p>
<p>StarMax 3000/200 Desktop	$1,995     $1,695     $300</p>
<p>StarMax 3000/200 Minitower    $2,195     $1,895     $300</p>
<p>StarMax 3000/240 Minitower    $2,795     $2,495     $300</p>
<p>StarMax 4000/160 Desktop	$2,295     $1,895     $400</p>
<p>StarMax 4000/160 Minitower    $2,895     $2,095     $800</p>
<p>StarMax 4000/200 Desktop	$2,995     $2,795     $200</p>
<p>StarMax 4000/200 Minitower    $3,195     $2,995     $200</p>
</text>
